        "id": 7127,
        "name": "drkrash1969",
        "username": "drkrash1969",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/d/eada6e/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-01-28T19:15:41.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>1) Suppose there is a +1 damage effect in play.&nbsp; Someone hits a hero for 2 points, increased to 3. That hero can re-direct the damage to another target.&nbsp; Would the damage be 3 or 4? My guess is 3 because the same damage is being re-directed.</p><p>2) But if the hero's effect was instead, \"when you take x damage, deal x damage to another target,\" would that then increase the damage to 4 because essentially a 3 point \"attack\" is being launched, which should increase to 4?</p><p>Sorry if this is confusing, but I've realized it comes up more often than I would have thought.</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:37:19.268Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 1,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 5.0,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 7125,
        "topic_slug": "added-damage-to-added-damage",
        "display_username": "drkrash1969",
        "primary_group_name": null,
